{{!-- The sizes attribute of a rubric's picture (about/rubric.hbs, in its foreach): the width the picture needs to cover
the cell, in the grid of src/css/about.css, which depends on the cell's position. One column below 40rem, two to
64rem (the first cell spans both), four after: the first cell is 2 × 2, the second 2 × 1, the third and the fourth
1 × 1 (the third spans two when it is the last), the following ones fill rows of four, except the last row, whose
cells widen to fill it (1, 2 or 4 columns: half a row stands for them).
The cells are about 220 to 275 px high (a row is 9 to 13.5rem, more when the text needs it): a 16:9 picture covering
one needs 1.78 times its height when that is more than the cell's width (max(...)): 440 px on a phone, 400 on a
tablet, 490 for a cell of one column of a desktop grid, 800 for the large first cell (2 rows). --}}
{{~#has number="1"~}}
  (max-width: 639px) max(92vw, 440px), (max-width: 1023px) 92vw, max(calc((92vw - 16px) / 2), 800px)
{{~else~}}
  {{~#has number="3"~}}
    {{~#if @last~}}
      (max-width: 639px) max(92vw, 440px), (max-width: 1023px) max(calc((92vw - 16px) / 2), 400px), (max-width: 1443px) max(calc((92vw - 16px) / 2), 490px), 656px
    {{~else~}}
      (max-width: 639px) max(92vw, 440px), (max-width: 1023px) max(calc((92vw - 16px) / 2), 400px), max(calc((92vw - 48px) / 4), 490px)
    {{~/if~}}
  {{~else~}}
    {{~#has number="4"~}}
      (max-width: 639px) max(92vw, 440px), (max-width: 1023px) max(calc((92vw - 16px) / 2), 400px), max(calc((92vw - 48px) / 4), 490px)
    {{~else~}}
      (max-width: 639px) max(92vw, 440px), (max-width: 1023px) max(calc((92vw - 16px) / 2), 400px), (max-width: 1443px) max(calc((92vw - 16px) / 2), 490px), 656px
    {{~/has~}}
  {{~/has~}}
{{~/has~}}
